<%# Who reads one Google connection, beside its account on /integrations (integrations/_google_connection) and /admin/google: "Your agents can read this" for the household's, "Your app's agent can read this when you chat with it" for a client app owner's own, "Only you can see this" for anyone else's. The words and the rule are GoogleConnection#who_reads, which mirrors the agent side's gate (AgentMessages::MemoryBundle), so the page says what the code does. Local: connection. %>
